    {
      "number": 1,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 6,
      "stem": "A fair coin is tossed twelve times independently. Let $X$ be the number of tails.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the probability that the numbers of heads and tails are equal.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find the probability that there are more tails than heads.",
          "marks": 3
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$X\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(12,1/2)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use$P(X=6)=\\binom{12}{6}(1/2)^{12}$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P(X=6)=0.2255859375\\approx0.226$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M2",
              "text": "By symmetry,$P(X\\ge7)=[1-P(X=6)]/2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P(X\\ge7)=0.38720703125\\approx0.387$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$X\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(12,1/2)$. $P(X=6)=0.2255859375\\approx0.226$. $P(X\\ge7)=0.38720703125\\approx0.387$.",
      "sourcePages": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 6,
      "stem": "The paired data are shown below. The unknown value $a$ is a whole number. A rounded equation of the least-squares regression line of $y$ on $x$ is $y=2.398x+101.446$.\n\n|$x$|12|15|17|28|$a$|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|$y$|127|142|144|171|151|",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find $\\bar y$.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "b(i)",
          "prompt": "Use the regression line and the fact that $(\\bar x,\\bar y)$ lies on it to estimate $\\bar x$, giving your result to the nearest whole number.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b(ii)",
          "prompt": "Hence find $a$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Calculate the product-moment correlation coefficient.",
          "marks": 1
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\bar y=735/5=147$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$147=2.398\\bar x+101.446$using the rounded line."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\bar x\\approx18.9967$, hence$\\bar x=19$to the required precision."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$(12+15+17+28+a)/5=19$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$a=23$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$r=398/\\sqrt{166\\cdot1026}=0.96439588\\ldots\\approx0.964$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$\\bar y=735/5=147$. $\\bar x\\approx18.9967$, hence$\\bar x=19$to the required precision. $a=23$. $r=398/\\sqrt{166\\cdot1026}=0.96439588\\ldots\\approx0.964$.",
      "sourcePages": [
        3
      ]
