      "marks": 6,
      "stem": "The diagram shows a differentiable function $f$. Point $A(2,3)$ is a stationary maximum. Define $g(x)=x^2+1$ and $h(x)=f(x)/g(x)$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "",
          "prompt": "Find an exact equation of the normal to the graph of $h$ at $x=2$.",
          "marks": 6
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$h(2)=f(2)/g(2)=3/5$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$h\\prime=(f\\prime g-fg\\prime)/g^2$."
