    {
      "number": 8,
      "section": "A",
      "marks": 8,
      "stem": "$ABCD$ is a square of side $6$ metres and $Q$ is its centre. Point $P$ is vertically above $Q$, with $PQ=3\\sqrt2$ metres. Two ants start at $P$ simultaneously: one moves along $PA$ at $1.5\\,\\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}$, and the other along $PB$ at $2\\,\\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}$. Their speeds remain constant.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Show that triangle $PAB$ is equilateral.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find the rate at which the distance between the ants is increasing after $40$ seconds. Work in centimetres and seconds.",
          "marks": 5
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$AC=\\sqrt{6^2+6^2}=6\\sqrt2$, so$AQ=BQ=3\\sqrt2$metres."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$PA=\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt2)^2+(3\\sqrt2)^2}=6$metres."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Similarly$PB=6=AB$, so the triangle is equilateral."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Let their travelled distances be$x,y$and separation$z$; $z^2=x^2+y^2-xy$because the included angle is$60^\\circ$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Differentiate with respect to$t$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$2z\\dot z=2x\\dot x+2y\\dot y-x\\dot y-y\\dot x$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "At$t=40$, $x=60$, $y=80$and$z=20\\sqrt{13}$cm."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\dot z=\\sqrt{13}/2\\,\\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\\approx1.80\\,\\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$PA=\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt2)^2+(3\\sqrt2)^2}=6$metres. Similarly$PB=6=AB$, so the triangle is equilateral. Let their travelled distances be$x,y$and separation$z$; $z^2=x^2+y^2-xy$because the included angle is$60^\\circ$. $2z\\dot z=2x\\dot x+2y\\dot y-x\\dot y-y\\dot x$. At$t=40$, $x=60$, $y=80$and$z=20\\sqrt{13}$cm. $\\dot z=\\sqrt{13}/2\\,\\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}\\approx1.80\\,\\mathrm{cm\\,s^{-1}}$.",
      "sourcePages": [
