    {
      "number": 9,
      "section": "B",
      "marks": 18,
      "stem": "Three planes are defined by $\\Pi_1:x-y+6z=1$, $\\Pi_2:2x+y=5$, and $\\Pi_3:3x+y+az=b$, where $a,b$ are real constants. Let $L=\\Pi_1\\cap\\Pi_2$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the acute angle between $\\Pi_1$ and $\\Pi_2$, in degrees.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find the acute angle between the positive $x$-axis and $\\Pi_1$, in degrees.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Find a vector equation of $L$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "d",
          "prompt": "When $a=4$ and $b=14$, find the common point of all three planes.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "e(i)",
          "prompt": "Use row operations or equivalent algebra to find $a$ and $b$ for which the three planes share infinitely many points.",
          "marks": 4
        },
        {
          "label": "e(ii)",
          "prompt": "For these values, state the set of common points.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "f(i)",
          "prompt": "Find the conditions on $a,b$ for which there is no common point.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "f(ii)",
          "prompt": "Under the conditions in part(f)(i), justify that $L$ is parallel to $\\Pi_3$.",
          "marks": 2
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use the normals$(1,-1,6)$and$(2,1,0)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\cos\\theta=1/(\\sqrt{38}\\sqrt5)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\theta\\approx85.8^\\circ$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "For a line-plane angle use$\\sin\\theta=|\\mathbf d\\cdot\\mathbf n|/(|\\mathbf d||\\mathbf n|)$with$\\mathbf d=(1,0,0)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\sin\\theta=1/\\sqrt{38}$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\theta\\approx9.34^\\circ$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "At$z=0$, $x=2,y=1$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\mathbf r=(2,1,0)+\\lambda(-2,4,1)$, $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The point is$(-5,15,3.5)$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Eliminate$x$from the second and third equations using the first."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The equations reduce to$y-4z=1$and$4y+(a-18)z=b-3$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Hence$(a-2)z=b-7$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Infinitely many common points require$a=2,b=7$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "It is$L:\\mathbf r=(2,1,0)+\\lambda(-2,4,1)$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "f(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$a=2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$b\\ne7$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "f(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$(-2,4,1)\\cdot(3,1,2)=-6+4+2=0$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The direction of$L$is perpendicular to the normal of$\\Pi_3$; inconsistency shows$L$is not contained in$\\Pi_3$, hence it is parallel and disjoint."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$\\cos\\theta=1/(\\sqrt{38}\\sqrt5)$. $\\theta\\approx85.8^\\circ$. $\\sin\\theta=1/\\sqrt{38}$. $\\theta\\approx9.34^\\circ$. At$z=0$, $x=2,y=1$. $\\mathbf r=(2,1,0)+\\lambda(-2,4,1)$, $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$. The point is$(-5,15,3.5)$. The equations reduce to$y-4z=1$and$4y+(a-18)z=b-3$. Hence$(a-2)z=b-7$. Infinitely many common points require$a=2,b=7$. It is$L:\\mathbf r=(2,1,0)+\\lambda(-2,4,1)$. $a=2$. $b\\ne7$. The direction of$L$is perpendicular to the normal of$\\Pi_3$; inconsistency shows$L$is not contained in$\\Pi_3$, hence it is parallel and disjoint.",
      "sourcePages": [
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "section": "B",
      "marks": 20,
      "stem": "The mass $R$ of a standard packet, in grams, is normally distributed with mean $500$ and standard deviation $18$. Packet masses are independent.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find $P(R<480)$.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find $P(R<500\\mid R>480)$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Find $c$ such that $P(R>c)=0.15$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "d",
          "prompt": "Five standard packets are selected independently. Find the probability that exactly one has mass below $480$ grams.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "e(i)",
          "prompt": "The mass $C$ of a premium packet is also normal. Its lower quartile is $724$ grams and its interquartile range is $52$ grams. Find its mean.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "e(ii)",
          "prompt": "Find the standard deviation of $C$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "f(i)",
          "prompt": "A further normal random variable $X$ has $E(X)=400$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X)=25$. Find $E(X^2)$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "f(ii)",
          "prompt": "Let $Y=3X+2$. Find $E(Y)$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(Y)$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "f(iii)",
          "prompt": "Let $Z=(X-400)/5$. State $E(Z)$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(Z)$.",
          "marks": 2
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P(R<480)=0.13326026\\ldots\\approx0.133$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$P(480<R<500)/P(R>480)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$(0.5-0.13326026\\ldots)/(1-0.13326026\\ldots)\\approx0.423$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use the0.85quantile of$N(500,18^2)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$c=518.6558\\ldots\\approx519$grams."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Let$B$be the number below480g."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$B\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(5,0.13326026\\ldots)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P(B=1)=5p(1-p)^4\\approx0.376$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "The upper quartile is$776$and the normal distribution is symmetric."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\mu_C=(724+776)/2=750$grams."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$P(C<724)=0.25$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$(724-750)/\\sigma=\\Phi^{-1}(0.25)=-0.67448975\\ldots$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\sigma=38.5477\\ldots\\approx38.5$grams."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "f(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$\\operatorname{Var}(X)=E(X^2)-[E(X)]^2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$E(X^2)=25+400^2=160025$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "f(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
