    {
      "number": 11,
      "section": "B",
      "marks": 18,
      "stem": "The curves $y=4\\cos x$ and $y=x^2$ enclose a finite region $R$ around the $y$-axis. Angles are in radians. A rectangle inside $R$ has vertical sides at $x=-a$ and $x=a$, with its upper vertices on $y=4\\cos x$ and lower vertices on $y=x^2$. The diagram is schematic.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the coordinates of the two intersections of the curves.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find the area of $R$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Find the volume generated when $R$ is rotated through $2\\pi$ about the $x$-axis.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "d",
          "prompt": "Find the volume generated when $R$ is rotated through $2\\pi$ about the $y$-axis.",
          "marks": 4
        },
        {
          "label": "e",
          "prompt": "Show that the area of the rectangle is $A(a)=8a\\cos a-2a^3$, and state the physically relevant interval for $a$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "f(i)",
          "prompt": "Show that the value of $a$ for the maximum area satisfies $\\displaystyle\\frac{\\cos a-a\\sin a}{a^2}=\\frac34$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "f(ii)",
          "prompt": "Find the maximum area of the rectangle.",
          "marks": 2
        }
      ],
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$(-1.201538\\ldots,1.443694\\ldots)\\approx(-1.20,1.44)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$(1.201538\\ldots,1.443694\\ldots)\\approx(1.20,1.44)$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Integrate upper minus lower between the intersections."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\int_{-\\alpha}^{\\alpha}(4\\cos x-x^2)dx$, where$\\alpha$comes from part(a)."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Area$\\approx6.30$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use washers with outer radius$4\\cos x$and inner radius$x^2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$V_x=\\pi\\int_{-\\alpha}^{\\alpha}(16\\cos^2x-x^4)dx$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$V_x\\approx74.2$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The bounding squared radius is$y$below$\\beta=\\alpha^2$and$[\\arccos(y/4)]^2$above it."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Split the disk integral at$y=\\beta$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$V_y=\\pi\\int_0^\\beta y\\,dy+\\pi\\int_\\beta^4[\\arccos(y/4)]^2dy$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$V_y\\approx8.83$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The base is$2a$and height$4\\cos a-a^2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$A=2a(4\\cos a-a^2)=8a\\cos a-2a^3$; a nondegenerate rectangle has$0<a<\\alpha$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "f(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$A\\prime(a)=8\\cos a-8a\\sin a-6a^2=0$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Rearrange to$8(\\cos a-a\\sin a)=6a^2$, then divide by$8a^2$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "f(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Solve the stationary equation in the physical interval and check against the zero-area boundary cases."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The maximum area is approximately$3.60$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "$(-1.201538\\ldots,1.443694\\ldots)\\approx(-1.20,1.44)$. $(1.201538\\ldots,1.443694\\ldots)\\approx(1.20,1.44)$. $\\int_{-\\alpha}^{\\alpha}(4\\cos x-x^2)dx$, where$\\alpha$comes from part(a). Area$\\approx6.30$. $V_x=\\pi\\int_{-\\alpha}^{\\alpha}(16\\cos^2x-x^4)dx$. $V_x\\approx74.2$. The bounding squared radius is$y$below$\\beta=\\alpha^2$and$[\\arccos(y/4)]^2$above it. $V_y=\\pi\\int_0^\\beta y\\,dy+\\pi\\int_\\beta^4[\\arccos(y/4)]^2dy$. $V_y\\approx8.83$. The base is$2a$and height$4\\cos a-a^2$. $A=2a(4\\cos a-a^2)=8a\\cos a-2a^3$; a nondegenerate rectangle has$0<a<\\alpha$. Rearrange to$8(\\cos a-a\\sin a)=6a^2$, then divide by$8a^2$. The maximum area is approximately$3.60$.",
